&lt;p&gt;In modern full-stack development, securing communication between a Single Page Application (SPA) and a REST API is a fundamental requirement. While stateless JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) are popular, relying on a single, long-lived token introduces a major vulnerability: if intercepted, an attacker retains access until expiration with no immediate revocation mechanism.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Shortening token validity to 15 minutes resolves this exposure, but causes abrupt logouts unless automated.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The standard architectural pattern is a &lt;strong&gt;dual-token lifecycle&lt;/strong&gt;: short-lived Access Tokens paired with longer-lived Refresh Tokens and automated silent interceptors.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In this tutorial, we will build a production-grade &lt;strong&gt;dual-token authentication system&lt;/strong&gt; using &lt;strong&gt;Spring Boot 3 (Spring Security 6)&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;React with Axios Interceptors&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  1. Dual-Token Architecture Overview
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Access Token (15 Minutes):&lt;/strong&gt; Passed in the &lt;code&gt;Authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;token&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; header on every HTTP request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Refresh Token (7 Days):&lt;/strong&gt; Stored securely and sent only to &lt;code&gt;/api/auth/refresh&lt;/code&gt; when an access token expires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Silent Renewal:&lt;/strong&gt; The React client catches &lt;code&gt;401 Unauthorized&lt;/code&gt; responses via an Axios response interceptor, fetches a fresh access token, and automatically retries the initial request seamlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;
text
[ React Client (Axios) ]                       [ Spring Boot 3 Backend ]
         |                                                 |
         | ----- POST /api/auth/login -------------------&amp;gt; | (Authenticates credentials)
         | &amp;lt;---- 200 OK { accessToken, refreshToken } ---- |
         |                                                 |
         | ----- GET /api/dashboard (Bearer AccessToken)-&amp;gt; | (Validates signature &amp;amp; expiry)
         | &amp;lt;---- 200 OK { protected data } --------------- |
         |                                                 |
   (15 min passes: Access Token expires)                   |
         |                                                 |
         | ----- GET /api/dashboard (Expired Token) -----&amp;gt; |
         | &amp;lt;---- 401 Unauthorized ------------------------ |
         |                                                 |
   (Axios Interceptor catches 401)                         |
         | ----- POST /api/auth/refresh (RefreshToken) --&amp;gt; | (Validates refresh token)
         | &amp;lt;---- 200 OK { accessToken: newAccessToken } -- |
         |                                                 |
   (Interceptor retries original request)                  |
         | ----- GET /api/dashboard (New AccessToken) ---&amp;gt; |
         | &amp;lt;---- 200 OK { protected data } --------------- |
