&lt;p&gt;The full-stack framework is officially stable and production-ready, supporting both React and Solid. It has already been used on millions of apps during its beta/RC phase. As its 𝕏 &lt;a href="https://x.com/tan_stack/status/2110022759338422327" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;launch video&lt;/a&gt; puts it: "Feels like building a SPA. With the whole server behind you".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Client-first:&lt;/strong&gt; SPA-style routing, state and caching, with server rendering, streaming and typed server functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Type-safe end to end:&lt;/strong&gt; route params, search params, loader data and server function inputs are all typed, keeping changes consistent for both humans and agents. Type checking speed has been thoroughly optimized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Agent-ready:&lt;/strong&gt; packages ship TanStack Intent skills, so agents can learn Start's APIs and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;RSC is opt-in:&lt;/strong&gt; supported, but the team removed it from tanstack.com because it made the codebase harder to reason about.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Deploy anywhere&lt;/strong&gt; with Vite and Nitro. Rsbuild is also supported.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;




&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 &lt;a href="https://dub.sh/3jnUg5C" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Lingui - React i18n macros now compile natively in Vite, 2.5x faster than SWC and nearly 30x faster than Babel&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💬 &lt;a href="https://github.com/reactjs/rfcs/pull/284" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;React RFC - React work counters&lt;/a&gt; - Suggests improving the production observability of React by exposing metrics such as number of re-renders, setState calls or commits. I like the idea of giving metrics for agents to hill-climb and optimize against.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👀 &lt;a href="https://github.com/mobxjs/mobx/pull/4735" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MobX PR - MobX React plugin&lt;/a&gt; - An upcoming bundler plugin will help MobX and the React Compiler coexist. Wraps components in &lt;code&gt;observer()&lt;/code&gt;, adds &lt;code&gt;"use no memo"&lt;/code&gt; directives, turns &lt;code&gt;async&lt;/code&gt; methods into MobX flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;👀 &lt;a href="https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/99628" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Next.js PR - &lt;code&gt;eslint-config-next&lt;/code&gt; supports ESLint 10&lt;/a&gt; - &lt;code&gt;eslint-plugin-react&lt;/code&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/jsx-eslint/eslint-plugin-react/pull/4022" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;still doesn't support ESLint 10&lt;/a&gt;, so Next.js 16.5 canary patches it in place. Next.js users can finally upgrade.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;🔐 &lt;a href="https://nextjs.org/blog/upcoming-nextjs-security-update-october-2026" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Next.js - Upcoming security update&lt;/a&gt; - Planned for October 14: 2 critical and 1 high severity vulnerabilities in upstream dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://jimmyhmiller.com/what-does-the-react-compiler-even-do" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Can we Make React Faster using the React Compiler?&lt;/a&gt; - Explains what the compiler outputs, how it works, and then prototypes various optimizations: component inlining, Million.js-style blocks, Solid-like list selection, automatic context and Zustand selectors...&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://mattrothenberg.com/notes/classname-considered-harmful/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;className Considered Harmful&lt;/a&gt; - How design systems drift when components accept &lt;code&gt;className&lt;/code&gt;, and how popular design systems restrict it. Why not a &lt;code&gt;DANGEROUS_className&lt;/code&gt; prop 🤔.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://bra31k.dev/en/blog/same-bytes-17-percent-faster" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;How we made a 9 MB WebAssembly module feel faster without removing a single byte&lt;/a&gt; - A chain of suspending components delayed the loading of a large WASM file. Preloading it made the first canvas render 15-19% faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://julesblom.com/writing/react-visual-notation" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;A visual notation for React's parent and owner trees&lt;/a&gt; - A diagram format for showing component structure, ownership, and context at a glance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;📜 &lt;a href="https://certificates.dev/blog/debugging-suspense-with-the-react-suspense-panel" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Debugging Suspense with the React Suspense Panel&lt;/a&gt; - A practical tour of the new React DevTools 8.0 Suspense tab.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;💸 &lt;a href="https://sentry.io/resources/201-session-replays/?utm_source=thisweekinreact&amp;amp;utm_medium=paid-community&amp;amp;utm_campaign=replay-fy27q3-sessionreplayworkshop&amp;amp;utm_content=newsletter-react-link-register" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Sentry - Stop scrubbing replays. Learn the sampling, filters, and React hooks that find the right session, live on Nov 5th. Save your spot&lt;/a&gt;
